[step] The 1 mm plane offset compares the 6 mm guide foot with the 7 mm full-thickness jaw shelf and coupling toes. The raised Z7 plane supports lower jaw D at assembled Z15. The shelf and toes extend down to the bed at Z0; their exposed rise above the foot is not a separate 1 mm wall or unsupported skin.
alternatives: Lowering the raised support plane to Z6 drops the collar and tube axis by 1 mm. Raising the entire 124 x 100 mm guide foot to 7 mm removes this offset but adds about 12.4 cm3 of material while leaving the 7 mm jaw-support and coupling-seat sections unchanged. The 6 mm guide foot and 7 mm support plane preserve the specified guide and tube datums.
