[sliver] This 1 x 32 mm exposed face is the end step of the narrow jaw shelf at X0, between Z6 and Z7. The shelf is solid from Z0 to Z7 across Y-16..16 and X-38.5..0, and prints directly on its broad bed face. The exposed 1 mm rise is supported by 7 mm stock; it is not an independent thin fin.
alternatives: Lowering the shelf to the 6 mm foot height loses the required Z7 jaw-support datum. Raising the complete 124 x 100 mm foot to 7 mm adds about 12.4 cm3 while preserving the same shelf thickness. Widening the forward shelf into a full-width block fills the required front-stop lanes at Y16.5..21 and their negative-Y counterpart.
file: hardware/printed-parts/fixtures/tube-insertion/tube-insertion-carrier.step
click: x=0.000 y=0.000 z=6.500

[thin] The 0.354 mm negative-Y ranking measures from the foot's X0 front face to the adjacent shelf corner at X0, Y-16, Z6. Both ends and the segment midpoint (0,-16.1735,5.966) lie ON the analytic boundary. At that midpoint, X+0.01 is solid and X-0.01 is air; the segment follows the open front boundary rather than crossing a 0.354 mm ligament. Analytic vertical sections give 6 mm foot stock and 7 mm stock just inside the shelf edge.
alternatives: A continuous 7 mm guide foot removes the opposing corner faces but adds about 12.4 cm3 without thickening the existing 7 mm shelf. Filling the forward gap beyond the 32 mm shelf intersects the fixed front-stop strip at Y-21..-16.5, X-4..0 at the seating limit. Lowering the shelf to 6 mm moves the collar off its required tube-axis height.
file: hardware/printed-parts/fixtures/tube-insertion/tube-insertion-carrier.step
