[thin] The 0.354 mm positive-Y ranking measures from the foot's X0 front face to the adjacent shelf corner at X0, Y16, Z6. Both ends and the segment midpoint (0,16.1735,5.966) lie ON the analytic boundary. At that midpoint, X+0.01 is solid and X-0.01 is air; the segment follows the open front boundary rather than crossing a 0.354 mm ligament. Analytic vertical sections give 6 mm foot stock and 7 mm stock just inside the shelf edge.
alternatives: A continuous 7 mm guide foot removes the opposing corner faces but adds about 12.4 cm3 without thickening the existing 7 mm shelf. Filling the forward gap beyond the 32 mm shelf intersects the fixed front-stop strip at Y16.5..21, X-4..0 at the seating limit. Lowering the shelf to 6 mm moves the collar off its required tube-axis height.
