[thin] The 0.373 mm negative-Y ranking measures from the foot's X0 front face to the inner corner of the adjacent coupling toe at X0, Y-30, Z6. Both ends and the midpoint (0,-29.9,5.8425) lie ON the analytic boundary. X+0.01 at the midpoint is solid and X-0.01 is air, so this distance follows the open front boundary. Vertical analytic sections give 6 mm foot stock and 7 mm stock immediately inside the toe. The ranking does not describe a 0.373 mm material bridge.
alternatives: Raising the whole guide foot to 7 mm removes these adjacent opposing faces and adds about 12.4 cm3; the coupling toe remains 7 mm thick. Joining the toe to the central shelf with a broad full-height web fills the required negative-Y stop lane at X-4..0, Y-21..-16.5. Lowering the toe to 6 mm loses the lower-jaw coupling support datum.
